cpYaoJ.description:
1. Swelling of tissue after prolonged contact with a fluid (e.g., maceration of skin after a long bath  → "washerwoman skin"); 
2. Softening of skin and detachment of the epidermis in a stillborn fetus;
3. A procedure in anatomy and forensic medicine that is used to prepare bones for examination by allowing the body to decompose in a closed-container;
4. A process in pharmacology in which an active ingredient is extracted from a substance (e.g., plant) by placing the substance in a special solvent.
